<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.9.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01413</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.9.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e95079d7-5769-41fc-8bb8-614709269598</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
        <exercise id="_61773217-5b27-4b8b-bfca-abc27475c09f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00001">The number of people with the flu during an epidemic is a function, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, of the number of days, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, since the epidemic began. The equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> defines <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. </para>
          
          <para id="para-00002">How many people had the flu at the beginning of the epidemic? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.</para>
       
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            
            <para id="para-00003">Try again. Revisit activity 5.9.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">The correct answer is 50 because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8f49e66b-5a03-4b16-99ef-0d156a165ea6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00005">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> mean in this situation?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00006">Try again. Revisit activity 5.9.2. 
    </para>
            <para id="para-00007">The correct answer is: The number of people infected 1 day after the epidemic began.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_88f841b1-5c27-4127-a0e9-d2f11e8db5c5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00008">The function, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math><emphasis>,</emphasis> gives the dollar value of a bond <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> years after the bond was purchased. The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is shown.    </para>
          <para id="para-00009">(<media alt="Graph of function."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_11_11_01.svg"/></media>)</para>
  
            <para id="para-00010">What is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            
            <para id="para-00011">Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2.
    </para>
            <para id="para-00012">The correct answer is 1000.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d38e53c0-9f96-4884-a292-16de37669801" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00013">When is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1500</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>? Estimate the nearest whole number. Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            
            <para id="para-00014">Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">The correct answer is 8.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="aa87cef9-a6e1-47db-8e21-1aab28675ffa" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00016">A function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gives the number of stray cats in a town <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> years since the town started an animal control program. The program includes both sterilizing stray cats and finding homes to adopt them. An equation representing <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>243</m:mn><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 0?
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            
            <para id="para-00018">Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2 – 5.9.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00019">The correct answer is 243.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_577e38c4-c993-4814-8eae-e434b4ce5220" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00020">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            
            <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2 – 5.9.3. 
    </para>
            <para id="para-00022">The correct answer is 81.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4f5580f5-59be-4273-862f-60c80bd2e0ee" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00023">Function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gives the amount of a chemical in a person’s body, in milligrams, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> hours since the patient took the drug. The equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> defines this function.</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Which is the best choice for the domain of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00025">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            
            <para id="para-00030">Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.3.
    </para>
            <para id="para-00031">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a44a2625-bc54-4d52-922f-2e0156f3ebe7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00032">Which is the best choice for the range of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00033">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            
            <para id="para-00038">Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.3.
    </para>
            <para id="para-00039">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>600</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>